{
  "id": "auditory-sensory-memory",
  "term": "auditory sensory memory",
  "definition": "Auditory sensory memory is the brief, automatic retention of sound information after it is heard, often described as echoic memory. In speech perception, how long this trace lasts can vary with properties of the sound and with a listener’s language experience.",
